%I A400883 #13 Oct 25 2026 19:00:02
%S A400883 2,23,311,4666,28843,153157,772888,3568900,16129531,70863234
%N A400883 Number of free polyominoes with 3n cells that can be trisected into three congruent polyominoes.
%C A400883 Each piece is necessarily an n-omino. "Congruent" means equal up to rotation, reflection and translation, so pieces may be mirror images of one another. We call such a polyomino "trisectable".
%H A400883 Dmitry Kamenetsky, <a href="https://puzzling.stackexchange.com/questions/139931/bisecting-and-trisecting-a-figure-in-multiple-ways">Bisecting and trisecting a figure in multiple ways</a>, Puzzling StackExchange.
%H A400883 Dmitry Kamenetsky, <a href="https://puzzling.stackexchange.com/questions/139926/dissecting-a-figure-into-three-congruent-pieces-in-three-different-ways">Dissecting a figure into three congruent pieces in three different ways</a>, Puzzling StackExchange.
%H A400883 Dmitry Kamenetsky, <a href="/A400883/a400883.png">Illustration of a(2) = 23: trisections and halvings of all 35 free hexominoes</a>.
%F A400883 A000105(n)/8 <= a(n) <= 64 * A000105(n) * (3n+1)^4.
%e A400883 a(2) = 23: a hexomino is trisectable iff it can be tiled by dominoes. For example (pieces A, B, C):
%e A400883   AAB    AB.    ABB
%e A400883   CCB    AB.    A.C
%e A400883          CC     ..C
%Y A400883 Cf. A399996 (two congruent pieces), A000105.
%K A400883 nonn,hard,more,changed
%O A400883 1,1
%A A400883 _Dmitry Kamenetsky_, Oct 08 2026
